## Implementation Spec: Fix Empty Modal Layout in UnifiedEditModal

### Task 1: Remove VerticalScroll wrapper and dock:bottom from CSS

**File**: `pipeline/tui.py`, lines 1189-1227 (UnifiedEditModal.CSS)

**Changes**:
1. Remove the entire `#unified-edit-dialog VerticalScroll { height: 100%; }` CSS rule (lines 1201-1203) — this rule causes the circular sizing dependency that collapses the scroll container to zero height.
2. Add `overflow-y: auto;` to the `#unified-edit-dialog` rule (after `max-height: 80%;`) — this ensures the outer Vertical still scrolls if content exceeds available height, matching the working NewFeatureModal pattern.
3. Remove `dock: bottom;` from the `#unified-edit-buttons` rule (line 1222) — docking removes buttons from normal flow which contributes to the layout issue. The buttons should participate in normal vertical flow like in NewFeatureModal.

**Concrete CSS after changes**:
```
CSS = """
UnifiedEditModal {
    align: center middle;
}
#unified-edit-dialog {
    width: 60;
    height: auto;
    max-height: 80%;
    overflow-y: auto;
    border: thick $panel;
    background: $surface;
    padding: 1 2;
}
#unified-edit-dialog Label {
    width: 100%;
    text-wrap: wrap;
    margin-top: 1;
}
#unified-edit-dialog Input {
    margin: 1 0;
}
#unified-edit-dialog Select {
    margin: 1 0;
}
#unified-edit-dialog TextArea {
    margin: 1 0;
    height: 4;
}
#unified-edit-buttons {
    margin-top: 1;
    height: 3;
}
#unified-edit-buttons Button {
    margin: 0 1;
}
"""
```

**Dependencies**: None

